<h1>ragged matrix</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="matrix.html"><em>matrix</em></a> having irregular numbers of items in each row.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="uniformmatrx.html"><em>uniform matrix</em></a>, <a href="sparsematrix.html"><em>sparse matrix</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
An <a href="upperTriangularMatrix.html"><em>upper triangular matrix</em></a> or a <a href="lowerTriangularMatrix.html"><em>lower triangular matrix</em></a> are usually not thought of as being ragged since the number of items in each row is regular (changing by one from row to row). 
<p> For example <table> 
<tr><td>1</td><td>16</td><td>18</td><td>9</td><td>12</td></tr> 
<tr><td>6</td></tr> 
<tr><td>1</td><td>8</td><td>3</td><td>0</td></tr> </table></em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

